{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Field","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Round","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.swPsi_zero_at_inv_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.swPsi_zero_at_inv_pow","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedThetaLimit.lean#L198-L206","doc":"`Ψ_SW(x) = ∏_{i<N} (1 − w^{i+1} x)` vanishes at `x = (w^m)⁻¹` whenever\n`1 ≤ m ≤ N`: the SW normaliser's continuation kills every negative index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.fract_logClass_E_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.fract_logClass_E_shift","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedThetaLimit.lean#L172-L181","doc":"**The class statement.**  The fractional part of `log_v` of any point of the\n`E`-shifted lattice `E v^m` is exactly `frac(log_v E)` — the class φ₁.  This is\nthe arithmetic content of \"the balanced tropical class is φ₁\": the integer part\nof the lattice index drops out, for every `m : ℤ`.  Combined with\n`balanced_dcoef_ratio`, it says the balanced `D`-function's tropical corners\ncarry class φ₁ exactly once the normaliser ratio tends to 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.logClass_E_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.logClass_E_shift","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedThetaLimit.lean#L162-L170","doc":"`log_v (E · v^m) = m + log_v E` for `v > 1`, `E > 0`, `m : ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.logClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.logClass","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedThetaLimit.lean#L158-L160","doc":"The `log_v`-class coordinate, written with `Real.log` (this is `Real.logb v x`;\nspelled out so the module does not need the `Logb` import). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.balanced_dcoef_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.balanced_dcoef_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedThetaLimit.lean#L138-L154","doc":"**The balanced coefficient ratio, division-free.**  Equivalent to\n`−d_j / d_{j+1} = E · w^{−(2j+1)} · g_j / g_{j+1}`: the `j`-th tropical corner\nof `D_bal` is `E w^{−(2j+1)}` times the normaliser ratio.  With `w = q̃⁻¹` the\ncorner is `E q̃^{2j+1} (g_j/g_{j+1})`, so — once `g_j/g_{j+1} → 1` — the corners\nlie on the `E`-shifted `q`-lattice whose `log_q̃`-class is `frac(log_q̃ E) = φ₁`\n(§4).  Stated over a generic `CommRing`; no inverses appear. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.dcoef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.dcoef","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedThetaLimit.lean#L133-L136","doc":"The normalised balanced Taylor coefficient\n`d_j = d₀ (−1)^j Ei^j w^{j²} g_j` (with `Ei = E⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.defect_index_base_change","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.defect_index_base_change","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedThetaLimit.lean#L121-L129","doc":"The `j`-th defect term of the SW argument carries the exponent\n`k(k+1) + jk`, again a triple-product index at base `w²`, now with argument\n`w^{j+2} u`: `k(k+1) + j·k = k(k−1) + (j+2)·k`.  Under hypothesis (H) of the\naudit the balanced defect has *literally this* expansion, with the SW\ncoefficients `(−1)^{j+1} w^{j(j+1)/2}/(w;w)_j` replaced by the Taylor\ncoefficients of the balanced normaliser. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.theta_index_base_change","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.theta_index_base_change","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedThetaLimit.lean#L112-L119","doc":"The recentred summand carries the exponent `k(k+1)`, which is a\nJacobi-triple-product index **at base `w²`**: `k(k+1) = k(k−1) + 2k`.  So the\nlimit `Σ_{k∈ℤ} (−1)^k w^{k(k+1)} u^k` is the theta function at base `p = w²`\nwith argument `w² u`, whose zero set is `u ∈ w^{2ℤ}` — the balanced tropical\nlattice.  This is *the same theta function* as in the SW core; only the\nprefactor (`g_∞` in place of `1/(w;w)_∞`) differs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.balanced_E_absorption","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.balanced_E_absorption","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedThetaLimit.lean#L90-L108","doc":"**The `E`-absorption.**  With `Ei` the inverse scale (`Ei = E⁻¹`), the\n`j`-th normalised monomial of `D_bal` evaluated at the `E`-shifted recentring\npoint `z = E w^{1−2n} u` is exactly the SW recentred monomial:\n\n    Ei^j · w^{j²} · (Ei⁻¹ · w^{1−2n})^j = w^{n−n²} · w^{(j−n)(j−n+1)} .\n\nThe `E`-dependence cancels identically — for every `j`, not asymptotically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.recentring_exponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedThetaLimit.recentring_exponent","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedThetaLimit.lean#L83-L88","doc":"The exponent bookkeeping: `j² + (1−2n)j = (n − n²) + (j−n)(j−n+1)`.\nIdentical to the SW core's `recentring_exponent`; recorded here because it is\nthe exponent that survives the `E`-cancellation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}